  "fidelity": {
    "functional": {
      "claims": "Nets, ports, the RGB LED, the power LED and the two buttons as parts; the ESP32-C3 runs its firmware from the flash image (see its description): its own ROM, the second-stage bootloader and the app, as on the board. RST pulls CHIP_PU low and the chip starts again with rst:0x1 (POWERON); BOOT held through it makes the ROM wait for a download (boot:0x4 (DOWNLOAD(USB/UART0/1)), waiting for download). The CP2102N's port is the session's console on UART0 (GPIO21/GPIO20) and a serial port on the host.",
      "omissions": [
        "the CP2102N itself: its USB enumeration, its VBUS sensing (R18, R19) and its supply current; its bytes reach UART0 directly, not as frames on GPIO20/GPIO21",
        "the auto-program circuit (Q1, Q2, R10, R12): a host's port has no modem lines here (a pseudo-terminal), so DTR and RTS stay deasserted and leave EN and IO9 alone, as a terminal that opens the port does; esptool's reset into download mode is not reachable through it (hold BOOT and press RST instead)",
        "the ROM's serial download protocol is the ROM's own, but esptool cannot reach it without the modem lines",
        "the USB's D+ and D- (to the CP2102N only: GPIO18 and GPIO19 are not wired to the connector, R2 and R3 unpopulated)"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "timed": {
      "claims": "As functional.",
      "omissions": [
        "as functional"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    },
    "electrical": {
      "claims": "The power path of the schematic: the USB's VBUS through D1 (a 1N5819) to 5 V, U2 (SGM2212-3.3) making 3V3 for the module, R20, the RGB LED and CHIP_PU's R5; D5 lit from 5 V through R11 (5.1 k); C6 (1 uF) with R5 (10 k) holding CHIP_PU low for some milliseconds at power-up; SW2 joins CHIP_PU to ground, SW1 GPIO9; R20 (10 k) holds GPIO8 high.",
      "omissions": [
        "the ESD diodes (D2, D3, D4) and the USB's 22 ohm and 0 ohm series resistors",
        "decoupling and bulk capacitors (C1, C2, C8, C9, C10, C12: with C1's 10 uF on the regulator's output the analog engine does not converge yet) and the unpopulated C4, C5, C13, C14, R2, R3, R14",
        "the bridge's supply current (the CP2102N's); the module draws its chip's (the ESP32-C3's supply table, ADR-036) but not its flash's own",
        "R17 (0 ohm) between GPIO8 and the LED: the LED's DIN is GPIO8's net",
        "the 1 uF on CHIP_PU makes the first 200 ms of a run slow: the analog engine steps its charge with the MCU's quanta (about 2.5 s of wall time)"
      ],
      "validation": [
        "tests/*.json"
      ]
    }
  },
